<!--Post: 1936--><!--Time: 1103146221-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1936"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Devbost<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Devbost<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 15, 2004 - 1:30 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->KAKE and Kansas.com are running almost identical straight news stories. It took a while, but ABC News and CNN are running stories on their respective sites. <BR> <BR>Interesting tidbit from KBSD, Channel 6: <a href="http://www.kbsd6.com/servlet/Satellite?pagename=KBSD/MGArticle/BSD_BasicArticle&amp;c=MGArticle&amp;cid=1031779685709">&#34;WSU crime expert says if authentic, latest BTK package is significant&#34;</a> <BR> <BR><b><i>“If it in fact, it is from the BTK strangler, it is a significant event,” said WSU criminologist Dr. Brian Withrow.  <BR> <BR>The package was found by a Wichita resident.  Reportedly, it contained what looks like Nancy Fox’s driver’s license.  <BR> <BR>“Serial killers cherish the items that they take from victims,” said Withrow.  “For him to relinquish that, it&#39;s really a significant thing because it just doesn&#39;t happen. “ <BR> <BR>Withrow says the manner this latest package was left is also unusual. <BR> <BR>“In all previous findings, he has left them in public places,” said Withrow.  “Receptacles - a book in a library, or a mailbox or a book drop in the library or places like that.  Leaving it out in the open in a field where somebody may or may not find it, it could&#39;ve been easily been picked up and put in the trash and been ignored.  It shows a degree of carelessness on his part.”</i></b> <BR> <BR>Carelessness, or just the appearance of it? If there&#39;s one thing BTK has never been, it&#39;s careless. It would be surprising for him to start slipping now - there&#39;s a good reason why he decided to leave the trash bag where it was. Just don&#39;t ask me what that reason is. <BR> <BR>From a message posted to the Wichita Eagle&#39;s <a href="http://www.kansas.com/mld/eagle/news/editorial/10415862.htm">feedback page</a>: <BR> <BR><b><i>I don&#39;t know who the police are trying to fool. I tried to call the BTK hotline. It rang 14 times, and nobody ever answered. <BR> <BR>The facts about BTK&#39;s identity are a joke. Don&#39;t investigators realize that those describe about 90 percent of 64- to 65-year-old men in this town?</i></b> <BR> <BR>I sincerely hope that the reason this person couldn&#39;t get through to the hotline is because the line was deluged with helpful tips. Otherwise, it&#39;s not very encouraging.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1936-->
<!--Post: 1938--><!--Time: 1103150190-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1938"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Colette<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Colette<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 15, 2004 - 2:36 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BTK called a convenience store to tell them about his park drop. Whatever the reason, no one went there then and the bag was found later.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1938-->
<!--Post: 1941--><!--Time: 1103153177-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1941"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Devbost<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Devbost<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 15, 2004 - 3:26 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hi Colette, <BR> <BR>I saw mention of this on another message board. I Googled for news stories that mention this angle, but came up empty so far. If you are able to provide a link, I&#39;d be most appreciative.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1941-->
<!--Post: 1950--><!--Time: 1103160540-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1950"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 15, 2004 - 5:29 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BTK is not careless. There is probably little or no camera surveillance at this park and/or the route in which he entered and departed. His drops will be more removed from populated areas. Some technology is not his friend: The good old days are gone. Each time he makes a drop people become more aware of areas that he is using. His spots are dwindling. Of course, he can drive out of town and use a mail drop. I am surprised that he has not left a package at the locations of some of his homicides, or contacted some of the survivors/living relatives. <BR> <BR>The convenience store employees may have thought that it was a joke or they were afraid of being victimized themselves. Some people do not care for the adrenalin rush.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1950-->
<!--Post: 1952--><!--Time: 1103161963-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1952"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:zodiacfiles@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Ed_neil<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ed_neil<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 15, 2004 - 5:52 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;m surprised he hasn&#39;t dropped letters in mailboxes at random &#40;or carefully chosen&#41; homes.  There can&#39;t be too many other places he can drop communications without being spotted now.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1952-->
<!--Post: 1953--><!--Time: 1103164947-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1953"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Doone<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Doone<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 15, 2004 - 6:42 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ed, that&#39;s an ingenious idea. I agree that the old killer is running out of options. And the last one&#40;near tree in park&#41;was not a success. <BR>But I&#39;m just glad the good samaritan called Kake instead of 911.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1953-->
<!--Post: 1960--><!--Time: 1103177457-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1960"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 15, 2004 - 10:10 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Serial murderers enjoy taunting the police and the public. Altering his typical delivery of evidence is part of manipulating them. It may appear careless with the possibility of someone viewing him being greater. The unknown subject most likely wore a disguise and took precautions. He does not want to be apprehended. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1960-->
